Extract tabular data from this census record text. This is an analysis pass over observed text; do not invent values that are not present in the text.
---
{{ observedText }}
---

Return a JSON object with this structure:
```json
{
  "title": "Brief description, e.g. '1850 US Census, Plymouth, Massachusetts, Sheet 3B'",
  "has_tables": true,
  "tables": [
    {
      "headers": ["Name", "Age", "Sex", "Occupation", "Birthplace", "Real Estate", "etc"],
      "rows": [
        ["John Smith", "45", "M", "Farmer", "Massachusetts", "$1200"],
        ["Mary Smith", "38", "F", "Keeping House", "Massachusetts", ""]
      ],
      "notes": "Enumerator: J.H. Wilson. Sheet 3B, Line 12-18."
    }
  ],
  "language": "en",
  "confidence": "high|medium|low"
}
```

Rules:
- Include EVERY household member present in the observed text
- Preserve all column headers exactly as written
- Use empty string "" for blank cells
- Mark illegible text as "[illegible]"
- Note the page number, line range, and enumerator if present
- Set has_tables: false if no tabular data found
{% else %}
No observed text is available. Return has_tables: false with a low-confidence explanation.
{% endif %}
